1. processor.js: a tool-call part stores the canonical TOOL_CALL_END.input
   as its arguments, including after the call is already input-complete, so
   a strict-mode null on an optional field never reaches validation.
2. tool-calls.js: while a step waits for approvals, a call that needs no
   approval runs now, like a client request, so no server call ends a run
   without its result.
3. error-payload.js: toRunErrorRawEvent keeps the provider's HTTP status next
   to the body it forwards, forwards an AWS service exception's name, fault
   side and status (it has no body), and forwards the status alone when the
   error has no body. `code` precedence (#985) is unchanged.
4. stream-to-response.js: flush TOOL_CALL_START before awaiting further
   provider output, so a stalled input still exposes its running tool card.
5. messages.js and ag-ui-wire.js: preserve reasoning provenance in UI/model
   conversions and AG-UI reasoning snapshots so replay decisions survive
   tool iterations and reload.
Upstream: still absent in @tanstack/ai 0.61.0. Remove each hunk when a
@tanstack/ai release does the same.

